{"records":[{"id":"f7btcr6x6d","title":"A non-canonical function of glutathione to suppress ferroptosis via FSP1","description":"Whole genome-wide CRISPR KO screen","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-10-02T11:41:52.925Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f7btcr6x6d","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f7btcr6x6d"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"BO","last_name":"CHU","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xn3vv2cdnk","title":"High-throughput CRISPR screens to dissect macrophage-Shigella interactions","description":"The positive hits, negative hits, and non-targeting controls of genome-wide CRISPR screens; Supplemental Tables.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-07-23T06:18:30.182Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xn3vv2cdnk","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xn3vv2cdnk"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yong","last_name":"LAI","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Genetic Screening","Host-Pathogen Interaction","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"33tm3dd9dw","title":"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery ","description":"Raw data deposited for \"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery\" by Djamshidi et al-Cell Reports Methods","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-09-25T15:53:30.358Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/33tm3dd9dw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/33tm3dd9dw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mahbod","last_name":"Djamshidi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Sanger Sequencing","Immunofluorescence"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"gbdfwg325y","title":"Bacteriostatic antibiotics promote CRISPR-Cas adaptive immunity against phages by enabling increased spacer acquisition","description":"Phages impose strong selection on bacteria to evolve resistance against viral predation. Bacteria can rapidly evolve phage resistance via receptor mutation, or using their CRISPR-Cas adaptive immune systems. Acquisition of CRISPR immunity relies on the insertion of a phage-derived sequence into CRISPR arrays in the bacterial genome. Using Pseudomonas aeruginosa and its phage DMS3vir as a model, we demonstrate that conditions that reduce bacterial growth rates, such as exposure to bacteriostatic antibiotics (which inhibit cell growth without killing), promote the evolution of CRISPR immunity. We demonstrate that this is due to slower phage development under those conditions, which provides more time for cells to acquire phage-derived sequences and mount an immune response. Our data reveal that the speed of phage development is a key determinant of the evolution of CRISPR immunity, and suggest that use of bacteriostatic antibiotics can trigger elevated levels of CRISPR immunity in human-associated and natural environments. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-11-04T13:32:56.091Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/gbdfwg325y","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/gbdfwg325y"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Tatiana","last_name":"Dimitriu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Microbiology","Antibiotics","Bacteriophage","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hfbhym45fz","title":"CRISPR screening reveals a requirement for ribosome recycling in efficient SARS-CoV-2 programmed ribosomal frameshifting and viral replication. Rehfeld et al.","description":"Supplemental Table S1. Results of SARS-CoV-2 programmed ribosomal frameshifting genome-wide CRISPR screens (MAGeCK analysis).\nSupplemental Table S2. Oligonucleotides.\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-01-19T12:17:58.922Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hfbhym45fz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hfbhym45fz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Joshua","last_name":"Mendell","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Frederick","last_name":"Rehfeld","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/0003xa228","name":"Cancer Prevention and Research Institute of Texas","grant_id":"RP220309"},{"id":"https://ror.org/00np6vq88","name":"Welch Foundation","grant_id":"I-1961-20210327"},{"id":"https://ror.org/006w34k90","name":"Howard Hughes Medical Institute","grant_id":null}],"categories":["Oligonucleotide","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"nxvdzybwhf","title":"Illuminating host-mycobacterial interactions with genome-wide CRISPR knockout and CRISPRi screens","description":"The data deposited here contains genome-wide CRISPR knockout and CRISPRi screen data, including the positive hits, the negative hits, and non-targeting controls. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-08-30T11:32:01.108Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nxvdzybwhf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nxvdzybwhf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yong","last_name":"Lai","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Functional Genomics","High-Throughput Sequencing","Tuberculosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"drkj8vhdms","title":"A study of Dynamics of synthetic yeast chromosome evolution shaped by hierarchical chromatin organization. Sijie Zhou et al.","description":"1.We comprehensively sequenced this SCRaMbLEd pool and detected over 260,000 rearrangement events via a loxPsym junction analysis method.By analyzing each rearrangement event, we uncovered a stable rearrangement landscape for synthetic chromosomes.\n2.To investigate the mechanisms underlying the rearrangement patterns,we compared the rearrangement map with local chromatin structures and the three-dimensional genome architecture via assay for transposase-accessible chromatin using sequencing (ATAC-seq) and genome-wide chromosome conformation capture (Hi-C), respectively","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-06-16T18:14:45.89Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/drkj8vhdms","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/drkj8vhdms"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Sijie","last_name":"Zhou","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Synthetic Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ptx3dzs926","title":"NGS data of CRISPR/dCas9 activation screen with CDK4/6 inhibitor Palbociclib in bladder cancer","description":"We used a genome-scale functional genomics approach to determine the mechanisms of resistance to PD0332991. Transcriptional activation was performed using the synergistic activation mediator (SAM) CRISPR-dCas9 library. Work flow: a) T24 cells with stably transduced SAM components. b) Low MOI lentiviral transduction of  amplified sgRNA library.  c)antibiotic selection for transduced  cells. e) divide cells into control(vehicle) and PD 7 days treatment. f) NGS of PCR amplicons. g) Comparison of sgRNA counts in control and treatment conditions.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-06-01T04:24:44.789Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ptx3dzs926","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ptx3dzs926"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhichao","last_name":"Tong","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"nnp5hdy9cv","title":"JDS 20936: “Genome-wide association study using haplotype libraries and repeated measures model to identify candidate genomic regions for stillbirth in Holstein cattle”","description":"Supplementary Files manuscript: JDS 20936 - “Genome-wide association study using haplotype libraries and repeated measures model to identify candidate genomic regions for stillbirth in Holstein cattle”.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-09-30T06:45:58.343Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nnp5hdy9cv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nnp5hdy9cv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Pablo Augusto de Souza","last_name":"Fonseca","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Angela","last_name":"Canovas","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Flavio","last_name":"Schenkel","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Bioinformatics","Animal Genetics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"jp2xgxgmpm","title":"Metabolomics","description":"The real-world efficacy, predictive biomarkers, and resistance mechanisms of Tumor Treating Fields (TTFields)-based triple therapy (combined with radiotherapy and temozolomide) in high-grade glioma (HGG) remain poorly defined. This study aimed to evaluate the survival benefit of triple therapy and identify genomic determinants of treatment response in the real-word cohort study.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-10-16T15:12:54.669Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/jp2xgxgmpm","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/jp2xgxgmpm"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Shanqiang","last_name":"Qu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Metabolomics"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":12298,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":40,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":12298,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":12252,"restricted":6,"embargoed":40},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":347},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":110},{"id":"ht